				"⠀⠀⠀⠀⠀",
				1003,
				1
			],
			"Message": "fix(Mountain): Correct method invocation on Client::SendNotification\n\nChange the invocation of `Client::SendNotification` from direct function call syntax to explicit trait method resolution (`::Fn`). The previous syntax failed to resolve correctly in the current compilation context, causing a build error when dispatching workspace folder deltas to the Cocoon extension host.\n\nThis ensures the notification `$deltaWorkspaceFolders` is successfully sent to the \"cocoon-main\" client upon workspace changes, adhering to the strict trait-based interaction patterns used in the Mountain backend.",
			"SHA": "5ae45559141de37b2e1ee90ac139df85a2e3412c"
		},
		{
			"Author": "Nikola Hristov",
			"Date": "2026-05-02T06:30:50Z",
			"File": [
				"⠀⠀⠀⠀⠀",
				1003,
				2
			],
			"Message": "refactor(Mountain): Flatten ExtensionState module structure\n\nRemove the wildcard re-export pattern and extensive header documentation in `ExtensionState/mod.rs`. Retain only the module declarations for `ExtensionRegistry`, `ProviderRegistration`, `ScannedExtensions`, and `State`, and add `#![allow(non_snake_case)]` to align with the canonical symbol resolution path `ExtensionState::State::State`.\n\nUpdate the `State` struct in `State.rs` to reference the full canonical paths for its nested fields (`ExtensionRegistry::ExtensionRegistry::Registry`, `ProviderRegistration::ProviderRegistration::Registration`, and `ScannedExtensions::ScannedExtensions::ScannedExtensionCollection`).\n\nThis continues the ongoing decomposition of `ApplicationState` into file-per-struct PascalCase modules, ensuring consistency with the recent flattening of `ConfigurationState`, `Keybindings`, `Decorations`, and `LifecyclePhase`.",
			"SHA": "3c93cebd36baa58fd1c4714394e2414898482cfa"
		},
		{
			"Author": "Nikola Hristov",
			"Date": "2026-05-02T06:30:31Z",
			"File": [
				"⠀⠀⠀⠀⠀",
				1003,
				1
			],
			"Message": "refactor(Mountain): Flatten ConfigurationState module structure\n\nRemove the wildcard re-export pattern and extensive header documentation in `ConfigurationState/mod.rs`. Retain only the module declaration for `ConfigurationState` and add `#![allow(non_snake_case)]` to align with the canonical symbol resolution path `ConfigurationState::ConfigurationState::State`.\n\nThis continues the ongoing decomposition of `ApplicationState` into file-per-struct PascalCase modules, ensuring consistency with the recent flattening of `LifecyclePhase`, `ScannedExtensions`, `ExtensionRegistry`, `Decorations`, and `Keybindings`.\n\nThe main struct now resides in its own canonical file, simplifying symbol resolution and adhering to the project's strict naming conventions.",
			"SHA": "32708523a69c6f4be56b25bbb180d46c4513dc9f"
		},
		{
			"Author": "Nikola Hristov",
			"Date": "2026-05-02T06:30:11Z",
